  "keyFindings": {
    "passiveWorkloadIncrease": "Headed trace-only measurement (zero synthetic probes) shows higher aggregate main-thread work on R4.2 during passive desktop idle and continuously visible ecosystem animation: H1 467.81ms -> 778.99ms (+66.5%) and H2 488.09ms -> 793.33ms (+62.5%) over 10-second windows, with increases in style recalculation, layout, and paint. The original headless benchmark substantially amplified this signal but did not invent it.",
    "mainThreadHeadroom": "Despite the increased aggregate work, no long tasks (>50ms) occurred in H1-H5 on either build. In H2 visible on R4.2, approximately 7.9% of the 10-second observation window contained recorded main-thread task activity (~92.1% free). These are CDP trace main-thread busy-time ratios, not OS CPU utilization measurements.",
    "userPerceivedSmoothness": "Real interactions are lighter on R4.2: continuous scroll (H4) -21.0% task time and -48.5% paint; planet hover (H5) -15.9% task time and -19.1% style recalc. Realistic pointer movement (H3 trace-only) was roughly neutral (+1.9%); burst instrumented pointer load was 26.0% lower on R4.2, and R4.2R S2 separately proved 95.0% burst write reduction (200 -> 10).",
    "lifecycleSuspension": "Targeted decorative animation timelines pause while the ecosystem is offscreen (data-eco-paused, R4.2R S4) and pause in the hidden state per deterministic visibilitychange logic simulation (R4.2R S5: bg_paused_attr=true, timelines paused, raf_while_hidden=0). The headed H7 real tab switch never reached a hidden state, so OS-level background suspension is not demonstrated by that artifact. No GPU/compositor/energy claims are made.",
    "headlessDiscrepancy": "Proven: adding benchmark instrumentation materially changes collected timing; trace-only and instrumented results differ; the headless benchmark produced substantially larger TaskDuration deltas than headed trace-only execution; the Chromium execution environment affects scheduling. Inferred (likely contributors, not isolated): headless compositing without hardware V-Sync, probe-script distortion (240 queued RAF callbacks, monkey-patched RAF counter, PerformanceObserver), and CDP cumulative-counter boundary effects over short windows.",
    "reconciliationVerdict": "R4.2 is certified as FDS_WEBSITE_R4_2_RUNTIME_HARDENED_LIVE_CERTIFIED_WITH_VISIBLE_WORKLOAD_TRADEOFF: no user-facing blocking/jank defect observed, real interactions responsive, lifecycle hardening works, and the known passive visible main-thread workload increase is documented. Certification does not mean passive rendering is cheaper than R4.1, that CPU usage decreased, or that GPU/power was measured."
  },
